      "content": "KMP Basics"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Our optimization with KMP becomes even more noticeable in cases of texts with repeating patterns."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Take the text \"ABABABAC\" and the pattern \"ABABAC\". The algorithm compares the pattern (length 6) with a substring of the same length."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Optimizing Pattern Matching with Repeating Patterns",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "We start by comparing the pattern \"ABABAC\" with the first six characters of the text \"ABABAB\"."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "We find that the first five characters match: \"ABABA\""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "However, the last character \"C\" of the pattern does not match the corresponding character \"B\" in the text."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "And, we can also notice from the comparison that the third character in the text is \"A\"."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "So, our pattern can start directly from the third character of the text, thus skipping one unnecessary comparison."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Starting Comparison Directly From the Third Character of Text",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "How does it work?"
    },
